From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:24:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 086/110] Save As onto a file open in another tab does not make
 them clones

Tabs without a link paired by their path, so saving a tab as a file
another tab had open made the two clones, and the next mirror could copy
one text over the other. Only linked tabs are clones now; the tabs of one
file in a session from before links were kept are linked on restore. The
other tab shows the file changed on disk, as for any outside change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

